    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "continuation": false,
      "heading_level": null,
      "md_text": "As shown in Figure 3.1, “Expansion Architecture Overview,” the expansion bus is implemented as backplane (an expansion box) which accept PICs (boards). The recommended number of PICs to a backplane is five.",
      "bbox": [
        800,
        304,
        2045,
        500
      ],
      "segment_id": "page_0070_seg_002"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "continuation": false,
      "heading_level": null,
      "md_text": "Due to timing considerations, it is not possible to daisy-chain more than two buffered backplanes without inserting wait states.",
      "bbox": [
        800,
        556,
        2025,
        650
      ],
      "segment_id": "page_0070_seg_003"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "continuation": false,
